  "instructions": [
    {
      "type": "step",
      "text": "Add milk to saucepan\nadd egg, sugar, salt, cornstarch (also some vanillin) and vanilla bean\nHeat on MED heat for about 5 minute while continuously stirring\nonce mixture thickens, place into bowl and cover with plastic wrap, set aside"
    },
    {
      "type": "step",
      "text": "for dough\nadd warm milk and yeast to bowl, whisk, add sugar, egg, vanilla- whisk\nadd softened butter, whisk\nadd flour slowly,\nmix until combined\nknead about 5 minutes or until basically smooth and not sticky\nlet sit out for an hour\neither place in fridge or use immediately (sitting in fridge is easier to handle)\nroll out dough pretty thin, 1/2 to 1/4 inch?\nspread on custard\nroll up\ncut thin!! with floss\nset on tray and cover with plastic for ~ 15 minutes, egg wash and add almonds if adding\nthen baked in air fryer @ ~335F for 8-10 minutes +"
    }
